{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrw5pcQjFuTGGVQKFhBw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`get_metadata_for_wheel()` now reads METADATA only from the wheel's root-level `*.dist-info` directory, so a vendored package's dist-info can no longer be picked up by mistake. The regression test is added and the 9 tests in `tests/test_pep658_support.py` pass. I did not run the rest of the suite, `mypy` or `hatch run lint:fix`.\n\n- **Fix (`src/fromager/candidate.py`):** only `X.dist-info/METADATA` entries one directory deep are considered. If more than one root-level dist-info exists, the wheel filename from the URL is parsed and the one matching its name and version is used. The name is compared in canonical form, so `test_package` matches `test-package`.\n- **Regression test:** `test_get_metadata_ignores_vendored_dist_info` builds a wheel that contains a vendored `other-2.0.dist-info` (in a subdirectory and also at the root) alongside the real one. It checks that the real package's metadata is returned.\n\nIf the wheel has only one root-level dist-info, I use it without checking its name or version against the filename. The issue suggested requiring `{dist_name}-{dist_version}.dist-info`. I held back because a wheel with an unusual dist-info name would then fail where it works today.\n\nI didn't commit anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5886,"cache_read_input_tokens":32653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5886},"output_tokens":432,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d6d12e0-0281-4c4b-8dbe-7a2a0a06e9e8","uuid":"f2c3aa47-5601-4667-a34c-ece69e22583f","timestamp":"2026-10-09T15:53:49.568Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrw5pK3zxBbURzsRtb3v"}
